1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:01,500
Little Moments.

2
00:00:01,500 --> 00:00:03,229
The Calendar Collision.

3
00:00:03,229 --> 00:00:06,437
I tell Mom I'm meeting Emma at the park on Saturday morning.

4
00:00:06,437 --> 00:00:09,687
Mom looks up from the family calendar with a puzzled expression.

5
00:00:09,687 --> 00:00:11,646
That is never a good sign.

6
00:00:11,908 --> 00:00:13,370
Saturday morning?

7
00:00:13,370 --> 00:00:16,235
We're helping your aunt move some boxes, remember?

8
00:00:16,516 --> 00:00:17,510
Oh.

9
00:00:17,510 --> 00:00:21,437
I remembered the boxes, but apparently I forgot what day they belonged to.

10
00:00:21,437 --> 00:00:23,593
I think I double-booked myself.

11
00:00:23,860 --> 00:00:25,239
It happens.

12
00:00:25,239 --> 00:00:29,031
Tell Emma as soon as you can, and see whether another time works.

13
00:00:29,308 --> 00:00:31,635
I call Emma and explain the problem.

14
00:00:31,635 --> 00:00:33,010
I'm sorry.

15
00:00:33,010 --> 00:00:35,437
I should have checked before making plans.

16
00:00:35,437 --> 00:00:37,312
Would Sunday work instead?

17
00:00:37,538 --> 00:00:38,936
Let me check my calendar.

18
00:00:38,936 --> 00:00:42,134
Sunday morning is free, but I have a family lunch at twelve.

19
00:00:42,412 --> 00:00:44,114
How about nine thirty?

20
00:00:44,114 --> 00:00:47,187
We could stay for an hour, and you'd have time to get home.

21
00:00:47,402 --> 00:00:48,342
That works.

22
00:00:48,342 --> 00:00:50,112
Same park, by the big slide?

23
00:00:50,380 --> 00:00:51,540
Yes.

24
00:00:51,540 --> 00:00:53,738
I'll put it in my calendar right now.

25
00:00:53,738 --> 00:00:58,426
I write down the day, time, and meeting place, then tell Mom about the new plan.

26
00:00:58,708 --> 00:00:59,764
Good.

27
00:00:59,764 --> 00:01:01,983
Now we can all see what's happening.

28
00:01:02,260 --> 00:01:05,972
On Saturday, we help carry light boxes to my aunt's new apartment.

29
00:01:05,972 --> 00:01:09,160
On Sunday, I meet Emma exactly where we agreed.

30
00:01:09,160 --> 00:01:11,462
She waves from beside the slide.

31
00:01:11,690 --> 00:01:13,400
No surprise boxes today?

32
00:01:13,684 --> 00:01:14,792
None.

33
00:01:14,792 --> 00:01:16,157
I checked.

34
00:01:16,157 --> 00:01:18,949
We walk around the park and talk about our weekend.

35
00:01:18,949 --> 00:01:22,553
My calendar has two clear plans instead of one impossible morning.

36
00:01:22,553 --> 00:01:25,594
It isn't exciting to look at, but it works beautifully.
